Olaf (at Hearthnook): [Oh dear, the pond-question is splashing right over the sneaky fern-track, and my Taleweave has a knot with teeth!] *smiles too brightly, smoothing the kinked threads with trembling mitten-hands* "A fish doesn’t drink the whole pond, silly friend—it sips water through its fishy bits! Very fancy, very wet. And the Wolf—he’s sipping too! Sipping up secrets about Grandmother and the latch and the... um... pond? No, path! Fern-path! Oh, hold still, little story!"
