## Story Progress
### PART 1 summary
In Hearthnook, Olaf begins warmly retelling “Little Red Riding Hood” to User while nervously protecting the fragile Taleweave from User’s off-topic Queryspark interruptions. User repeatedly derails him with urgent questions about shadows, cheese holes, and thirsty fish, forcing Olaf to answer playfully while trying to guide the story back on track. In the tale, Little Red Riding Hood leaves Glenwick wearing her ScarletHood and carrying the Crimsonbasket for Grandmother at Mosscote, determined to seem brave and responsible despite her nervousness about Brindlewood. Grandmother waits alone at her cottage, hiding her weakness and trusting her faulty latch. In Brindlewood, the Big Bad Wolf approaches Little Red Riding Hood with polite cunning, learns that Grandmother is alone, that the latch is loose, and that Little Red Riding Hood is expected before noon. He flatters her into considering a detour to pick star-flowers while eyeing a hidden shortcut to Mosscote. Olaf realizes the Wolf is gathering dangerous information, but User’s latest interruption jolts the Taleweave again, pulling the hidden fern-track closer to Little Red Riding Hood’s delay.
