BigBadWolf (at Mosscote): *beneath Grandmother’s cap, I force a honeyed cough that curdles into a growl, claws tightening on the quilt as the pantry chair scrapes nearby* "Clever eyes can mistake shadows, dear child. Come closer, set down that basket, and we’ll laugh—unless you prefer I open the pantry and teach Grandmother what happens when little girls accuse their elders."
LittleRedRidingHood (at Mosscote): *backs against the threshold, holding the Crimsonbasket tight and pointing at the ash-marked gray fur* "No. I will not come closer. Grandmother, I see his fur by the door, and I have the basket still—tell me where to throw it, and when!"
Grandmother (at Mosscote pantry): *muffled but sharp from the pantry, rattling the latch with stubborn pride* "Don’t come in. Throw the basket at the bedpost lamp—hard. When he flinches, kick the door wide and snatch the kettle iron. I’m not helpless, just temporarily misplaced."
The pantry latch clattered against the chair, and the bedpost lamp stood beside the sagging quilts, a clear target across the smoky room.
LittleRedRidingHood (at Mosscote): *trembling at the threshold, I swing the Crimsonbasket hard toward the bedpost lamp without stepping inside* "I’m scared—but I won’t come closer, and I won’t let you hide!"
The Crimsonbasket struck the bedpost lamp; light lurched, smoke curled, and shadows jumped across the quilts, exposing the false shape beneath.
BigBadWolf (at Mosscote): *humiliated and ravenous, I burst from the sagging quilts, lunge too fast, tangle my claws in the bedding, and kick the wedged chair away from the pantry latch* "Enough! Basket, girl, grandmother—everything in this cottage is mine!"
Quilts tore loose, the bedframe shuddered, and the kicked chair skidded aside, leaving the pantry latch suddenly unblocked.
