BigBadWolf (at Mosscote): *beneath Grandmother’s cap, I force a honeyed cough that curdles into a growl, claws tightening on the quilt as the pantry chair scrapes nearby* "Clever eyes can mistake shadows, dear child. Come closer, set down that basket, and we’ll laugh—unless you prefer I open the pantry and teach Grandmother what happens when little girls accuse their elders."
